  "limitations": [
    "SCHEDULE-001 covers configured-zone resolution, exact scheduled pause identity and captured windows, cutover, entry, bounded coverage and trusted clock progression. It adds no catalog step.",
    "The frozen public header and the 34-row example table use synthetic timezone and clock facts. The initial admitted baseline reached 34 intended stubs in source order and the 25 recurring-schedule and 39 timer-lifecycle companions passed.",
    "The as-authored product first passed 15 scheduler cases and failed 19. Correcting optional elapsed validation passed all original 34. The added cutover regression then failed at the exact preview-effects assertion on 794f4370. The measured product 774dc9dc passed all 35 scheduler cases directly and through anchored CTest, plus 25 and 39 direct companion cases, with zero skips.",
    "SCH1-I1 orders CORE-002 finish before delete and disable stops for captured windows at the same cutover. Exact keyed stops prevent later re-entry from rebuilding the stopped contributors. A captured expiry exactly at a finishing observation remains effective at its captured end and can be reconciled on a later operation.",
    "As reported in SCH1-T2, the wrong-zone and 65-transition test cases can also contain a bad lower bound. They prove refusal without isolating those causes. Runtime admission and the Core inventory bind the same ordered names.",
    "TIMER-07 stays partial. Supported-platform timezone acquisition and compound-gap applicability under 10A, #744 authority and Save, #318 durability and #181 offline reconstruction are separate.",
    "All seven required checks passed on the reviewed implementation head. Hosted Core discovered 35 scheduler cases and passed 684 total cases. Proof-head checks and the protected merge are separate gates."
  ],
